    // So rotated string = s[k:] + s[:k]
    // Last character of rotated string = s[k-1] if k > 0, else s[length-1].
    // In general, last char = s[(k-1) % length] for k >= 1, and s[length-1] for k=0.
    // This can be written as s[(k-1+length) % length] for all k >= 0 if we handle k=0: (0-1+length) % length = (length-1) % length = length-1. Yes!

    // So for rotation by k (0-indexed, k from 0 to n-1), the last character is s[(k-1+length) % length].
